  <prompt>Delete the shared-tier BFF app-registration code and constants; H3 creates each customer's BFF app (D-13).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer (PowerShell, provisioning skill). Follow the provisioning constraints.</role>

  <goal>
    No script, constant, skill step or doc creates, names or requires a shared "Spaarke BFF - Trial 1" / "Spaarke BFF - Model 1"
    app registration, and /provision-environment no longer hard-stops on `bffApiAppId`. The container-type owning-app path
    (`-CreateOwningApp Model1`, FIC helpers, `-AcctClaimOnly`) and `containerTypeId` stay.
  </goal>

  <justification>
    <existing>Register-EntraAppRegistrations.ps1 `-CreateBffApp` (Trial1|Model1|Model2), Get-SpeTopologyBffAppDisplayName, New-SpaarkeSpeBffApp; spaarke-constants.yaml bffApiAppId / bffProdBase / name_templates.bffAppServiceRg + bffAppServiceName; SKILL Step 0.5b/0.5c reads them.</existing>
    <extension>Removal only; H3 (GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner, `spaarke-bff-api-{customerId}`) already owns the per-customer BFF app.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>SKILL Step 0.5c hard-stops every dispatch because bffApiAppId is null and no Model 1 stamp will ever have a shared one; an operator following the runbook creates an app registration nothing uses.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

